      "id": "void-overdrive-context",
      "type": "text",
      "width": "full",
      "heading": "The fantasy worked. the loop did not.",
      "body": "Void Overdrive began as a single-player hoverbike prototype and quickly became a multiplayer test bed for an open world. We rebuilt the hoverbike and networking stack in Unreal as well as Unity to understand the tradeoffs between engines; Unity ultimately gave us a stronger path for moment-to-moment gameplay.\n\nThe unresolved problem was the game itself. Fast traversal and the pleasure of exploring a huge landscape pulled toward immediate action, while the experience we wanted—maintenance, costly pursuit and slow, methodical survival—pulled the other way. We did not find a gameplay loop that reconciled those two experiences. That tension is the most useful part of the project now.",
      "source": "",
      "mediaRef": "",
      "href": "",
      "label": "",
